SUMMARY:Theatre Diaspora Presents: A Staged Reading of Edith Can Shoot Things and Hit Them
DESCRIPTION:Join us at the Literary Arts Bookstore & Cafe for a staged reading of Edith Can Shoot Things and Hit Them by A. Rey Pamatmat\, directed by Terry Kitagawa. \nThis event is free and open to the public. \nIf you plan to attend\, RSVP on Eventbrite here. \n\nAbout the book:  \nFilipino-American siblings Edith and Kenny are all but abandoned by the adults in their lives. Left to their own devices on a farm in remote Middle America\, the two kids have learned to rely on each other to survive. But when Kenny’s friendship with his classmate Benji becomes something more\, the outside world of adults threatens to shatter the home they have created. \n 
URL:https://literary-arts.org/event/theatre-diaspora-presents-a-staged-reading-of-edith-can-shoot-things-and-hit-them/
LOCATION:Literary Arts
CATEGORIES:Free Events,Bookstore
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://literary-arts.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Theatre-Diaspora_600x900-scaled.jpg
GEO:45.5213897;-122.6810304
END:VEVENT
